  "report_text": "The monthly number of solar flares increased steadily from February 2021 to February 2026, with a peak in February 2021.\nThe share of strong flares (GOES class M or X) showed a gradual increase over the years, indicating a rising trend in intense solar activity.\nThe busiest month was February 2021, with a count of 122 flares.\nThe number of flares per year increased each year, with the highest concentration in early years.\nThe percentage of strong flares rose from year to year, culminating in a higher proportion in 2025.\nThis suggests increasing solar activity over time, possibly linked to solar cycle dynamics.\nThe data shows a clear upward trend in both flare frequency and intensity, consistent with solar cycle progression."
